\title{mdbx: Bindings to the 'libmdbx' Embedded Key-Value Store}
\description{
Provides low-level bindings to 'libmdbx', a compact and fast transactional key-value store built on memory-mapped files (\url{https://libmdbx.dqdkfa.ru/}). Database environments, transactions, and byte-oriented read and write operations are exposed directly. The 'libmdbx' sources are bundled and compiled into the package, so no system library installation is required.
}
\section{Getting started}{


Data lives in an \emph{environment} — a file on disk, opened with
\code{\link[=mdbx_env_open]{mdbx_env_open()}} and closed with \code{\link[=mdbx_env_close]{mdbx_env_close()}}. Every read and write
happens inside a \emph{transaction}: \code{\link[=mdbx_with_read]{mdbx_with_read()}} and \code{\link[=mdbx_with_write]{mdbx_with_write()}}
open one, run your code and end it, committing if the block returns and
aborting if it throws. \code{\link[=mdbx_txn_begin]{mdbx_txn_begin()}} gives you the same thing by hand
when you need to decide at the end whether to keep the writes.

Within a transaction, \code{\link[=mdbx_get]{mdbx_get()}}, \code{\link[=mdbx_put]{mdbx_put()}} and \code{\link[=mdbx_del]{mdbx_del()}} address
single records, and \code{\link[=mdbx_keys]{mdbx_keys()}} and \code{\link[=mdbx_items]{mdbx_items()}} list what is there.
}

\section{Keys and values are bytes}{


'libmdbx' stores byte strings and records no type. A \code{raw} vector is stored
as-is; a single string is stored as its UTF-8 bytes, so \code{"k"} and
\code{charToRaw("k")} are the same key. Reads decode back to text by default and
fail rather than corrupt anything if the bytes are not text — pass
\code{as = "raw"} for values written with \code{\link[=serialize]{serialize()}}. A key that is not there
reads as \code{NULL}.

Serialization of arbitrary R objects is deliberately outside this package.
}

\section{The rules that are not obvious}{

\itemize{
\item \strong{One transaction at a time per environment.} Concurrency comes from
separate processes, and an environment does not survive a \code{fork()}. See
\link{mdbx-concurrency}, which is worth reading before using this package with
\pkg{parallel} or \pkg{future}.
\item \strong{Every commit is durable by default.} \code{\link[=mdbx_flags]{mdbx_flags()}} describes the flags
that trade that for speed, and what each one costs.
\item \strong{Closing is refused while a transaction is open}, because closing
underneath one is undefined behaviour in 'libmdbx'.
}

\code{\link[=mdbx_env_stat]{mdbx_env_stat()}}, \code{\link[=mdbx_env_info]{mdbx_env_info()}} and \code{\link[=mdbx_version]{mdbx_version()}} report on a
database and on the bundled library.
}

